**Diagnosis.** All five failures are semantic/execution issues the incumbent never checks: (a) exact string literals that don't match stored values (`'Bachelors'`, `'The Rise of the Blue Beetle'`, trailing-space `'%Korea %'`), (b) wrong column selection for "which countries / details" questions (gold returns all columns), (c) a negation query returning nothing because the relationship is stored in one direction only. The harness makes exactly one call and never uses `env.execute`, so none of these are ever caught even though `max_calls=2` allows a repair turn.

**Edit plan (3 edits).** (1) Rewrite `solve.py`: draft → execute → if error or zero rows, send a compact second-turn repair message containing the executed SQL, its result/error, and targeted diagnostics (actual stored values for each quoted literal via LIKE probes, plus an OR-both-directions probe when the draft filters on a single side of a relation). Deterministic fallback keeps the draft if repair fails. (2) Sharpen `system_prompt.md` with general rules for value matching, column-set choice ("which X" → all columns of X; explicit lists → exactly those), symmetric relations, and ties/LIMIT. (3) Raise `max_tokens` to 1000 so reasoning + final SQL aren't truncated.

